course: dictionary
lesson: 9153
title: Snooze and the snooze button
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A snooze is a short, light sleep, often in the daytime. Grandad snoozes in his armchair after lunch, and cats snooze in the sun. The clues are the times and places: after lunch, in the sun. Snooze is an informal word, so you will hear it in chatty talk more than in formal writing.
explain: Snooze can also be a noun, as in «have a snooze». On an alarm clock or phone, the snooze button stops the alarm for a few minutes. Look at the words around it: alarm, button, minutes. These clues show you that this meaning is about the alarm, not about sleeping in a chair.
explain: Read this sentence: «Snoozing an alarm gives broken, light sleep, and many people feel more tired after lots of snoozing.» Broken and light are the clues. They tell you the sleep is not deep or steady, so snoozing does not leave you rested. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
explain: The saying «you snooze, you lose» is a joke about being slow. If you are slow, you miss your chance. Here snooze does not mean sleep at all. Always check the words around the word before you decide what it means.
fact: Snooze means to have a short, light sleep, especially in the daytime.
fact: A snooze is a short sleep or a nap.
fact: The snooze button on an alarm clock or phone stops the alarm for a few minutes.
fact: «You snooze, you lose» means if you are slow, you miss your chance.
fact: «Snoozing gives a few more minutes, but the sleep is broken and many people feel more tired.» So snoozing does not mean you are fully rested.
exercise: «Grandad snoozes in his armchair after lunch.» What does snoozes mean here? | Shouts at the television | Cooks a big lunch | Goes for a long walk | *Has a short, light sleep
exercise: «Snoozing gives a few more minutes, but the sleep is broken and many people feel more tired.» What does this suggest about snoozing? | Snoozing is the same as getting up early | *Snoozing does not leave you fully rested | Snoozing always makes you wide awake | Snoozing makes the alarm ring louder
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Snoozing an alarm gives broken, light sleep.» that describes a sleep that is not deep. | snoozing | *light | people | alarm
test: Ella says «you snooze, you lose» is about sleeping. What does it really mean? | Sleeping is the best way to be healthy | *If you are slow, you miss your chance | Alarm clocks are always wrong | If you sleep too long, you win a prize
test: What does hit the snooze button mean? | Turn the alarm clock off for the whole day | *Stop the alarm for a few minutes | Wake up and jump out of bed at once | Make the alarm ring louder
exam: What does snooze mean in «cats snooze in the sun»? | To run quickly across the garden | *To have a short, light sleep | To eat a big meal | To stop an alarm for ever
